<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5546" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Bŏmilcar</span></b> ,
		ăris, m.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Carthaginian general</i>, <i>contemporary with Agathocles</i>, <i><span class="en">Just. 22,
				7, 8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>One of Hannibal</i>'<i>s
			generals</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 23, 41, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">24, 36, 7
			al.</span></i>—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A companion of Jugurtha</i>, <i>afterwards guilty of rebellion</i>, <i>and put to
				death by him</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. J. 35</span></i>; <i><span class="en">61</span></i>; <i><span class="en">62</span></i>; 70 sqq.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
